# face_clear.cam — the Clear takes a Face (Phase 61 slice 1; DECISIONS.md →
# "Phase 61 slice 1: a Clear takes a Plane and a Face…").
#
# A Face is a floor whose wall is the stock: the loop is the boundary, every
# edge of it open, and the Post standing through it is its island, derived
# from containment — nobody names it. The Clear is the VOLUME verb: it roughs
# everything above the floor, around the Post, leaving its one allowance on
# the Post's flank (the Side that follows takes it) and on the FLOOR too,
# because an End on the same Face follows and takes it (`derive_floor_skin`).
# Take the End away and the Clear cuts to the floor's z: nothing declares a
# floor that serves the part, so nothing is left on one.
#
# Two levels (`stepdown=3` over the 5.5 above the skinned floor). Both floor ops are unpinned; the
# Clear is the offset family, the End is spine.
units mm
feed 800
plunge 300
rapid_z 5
clearance_z 25
spindle 3000

stock Box(w=120, l=100, h=20, x=0, y=0, z=0)

tool T5 Endmill(dia=10.0)

feature Floor Face(z=-6
    loop
        10 10
        110 10
        110 90
        10 90
)
feature Post ProfileBoss(extent=6
    50 40
    50 60
    70 60
    70 40
)

run Clear(tool=T5, profile=Floor, stepover=4.0, stepdown=3, stock_to_leave=0.5)
run End(tool=T5, surface=Floor, stepover=4.0)
run Side(tool=T5, surface=Post, comp=control)
